WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:09.730 --> 00:00:13.611
Hey youtubers it’s charlie, everyone’s
been asking me for my sign of three breakdown

00:00:13.611 --> 00:00:14.611
so here it is.

00:00:14.611 --> 00:00:18.190
I ended up finding some really good references
and clues.

00:00:18.190 --> 00:00:24.680
also, since I posted my q&amp;a video steven moffat
and mark gatiss have started commenting on

00:00:24.680 --> 00:00:25.789
the future of the series.

00:00:25.789 --> 00:00:27.410
Next week is the finale his last vow and I’ll
be doing all the regular videos for that too.

00:00:27.410 --> 00:00:28.410
a review, a q&amp;a and then a breakdown.

00:00:28.410 --> 00:00:29.410
But I’ll also do a series 4 predictions.

00:00:29.410 --> 00:00:31.269
Be sure to subscribe to get all that stuff.

00:00:31.269 --> 00:00:35.060
Get excited too, because steven moffat said
that he and mark gatiss have plotted out all

00:00:35.060 --> 00:00:36.620
the way through series 5.

00:00:36.620 --> 00:00:38.680
That’s two more years of new sherlock.

00:00:38.680 --> 00:00:40.690
So just like last time this will be a relatively
chronological breakdown of all the references

00:00:40.690 --> 00:00:41.690
and most interesting bits of the sign of three.

00:00:41.690 --> 00:00:45.239
It will be super spoilery, so careful if you
haven’t seen the episode yet.

00:00:45.239 --> 00:00:47.730
Everybody grab your eyeball tea and let’s
get started.

00:00:47.730 --> 00:00:50.070
Number 1 - happy birthday sherlock.

00:00:50.070 --> 00:00:53.800
So it’s not exactly part of the episode,
but the monday after this episode aired was

00:00:53.800 --> 00:00:56.719
the 160th birthday of the sherlock holmes
character.

00:00:56.719 --> 00:00:58.390
He doesn’t look a day over 30.

00:00:58.390 --> 00:01:00.489
2 - The Red Headed League.

00:01:00.489 --> 00:01:04.080
The gang that lestrade and donovan are chasing
in the opening scenes is a reference to the

00:01:04.080 --> 00:01:05.340
red headed league.

00:01:05.340 --> 00:01:08.149
Also denoted by the red heading on the newspaper
article.

00:01:08.149 --> 00:01:12.289
In holmes canon the league was a ruse created
by bank thieves as a way to distract the authorities.

00:01:12.289 --> 00:01:16.340
One of the bank robbers from the original
story is named archie, the same name as the

00:01:16.340 --> 00:01:19.890
little boy sherlock promised to show the pictures
of beheadings to at the wedding.

00:01:19.890 --> 00:01:24.170
3 - The best theory i’ve seen about the
gang is that one of them is a member of scotland

00:01:24.170 --> 00:01:27.450
yard, which is how they stay ahead of lestrade.

00:01:27.450 --> 00:01:30.899
And that the three gunman from rikenback fall
are part of the clown gang.

00:01:30.899 --> 00:01:35.170
If you look at the pictures of each of them
they look somewhat similar to mrs hudson,

00:01:35.170 --> 00:01:36.170
watson and lestrade’s gunman.

00:01:36.170 --> 00:01:39.910
We don’t see one that looks like lestrade’s
gunman at the crime scene, but it’s implied

00:01:39.910 --> 00:01:44.380
that he was the one who kidnapped the little
girl who screamed at sherlock.

00:01:44.380 --> 00:01:48.830
See how much he looks like the person walking
into the school while sherlock was mind palacing.

00:01:48.830 --> 00:01:55.140
And since he looks amazingly like the background
policeman working with lestrade, we can guess

00:01:55.140 --> 00:01:58.800
that he is the inside man tipping off the
bank robbers.

00:01:58.800 --> 00:02:03.080
4 - When donovan tells lestrade that jones
will get all the credit, it’s a book reference

00:02:03.080 --> 00:02:05.979
to Athelney Jones from the original book sign
of four.

00:02:05.979 --> 00:02:09.560
During that book, jones arrested a family
but turned out to be wrong.

00:02:09.560 --> 00:02:14.900
So it’s possible that this waters gang lestrade
mentioned is innocent and the real villains

00:02:14.900 --> 00:02:17.800
are moriarty’s gunmen.

00:02:17.800 --> 00:02:20.239
Now working for the new villain charles agustus
magnussen.

00:02:20.239 --> 00:02:23.520
I’m expecting episode 3 to pay off this
bank robber plot.

00:02:23.520 --> 00:02:25.739
5- There’s blackmail afoot.

00:02:25.739 --> 00:02:29.540
The villain magnussen is based on the book
character charles augustus milverton.

00:02:29.540 --> 00:02:30.540
A master blackmailer.

00:02:30.540 --> 00:02:33.400
Here’s where things get weird with these
bank robbers.

00:02:33.400 --> 00:02:34.930
Notice the really old looking one.

00:02:34.930 --> 00:02:39.069
There’s a conspiracy theory this gang member
is actually mary morstan’s father.

00:02:39.069 --> 00:02:43.239
And mary has been living under a false name
and the villain has been using her father’s

00:02:43.239 --> 00:02:45.849
criminal identity as a means to blackmail
her.

00:02:45.849 --> 00:02:49.900
Think about what sherlock saw when he deduced
her, she’s a liar, she had a guardian and

00:02:49.900 --> 00:02:51.200
she has a secret.

00:02:51.200 --> 00:02:54.739
During sign of three she talks about being
an orphan, what if she’s lying about that

00:02:54.739 --> 00:02:56.430
and about her name.

00:02:56.430 --> 00:03:00.560
6 - More evidence mary’s real father is
a bank robber.

00:03:00.560 --> 00:03:04.569
In the original book sign of four, mary’s
father was involved with the stolen treasure

00:03:04.569 --> 00:03:05.569
plot.

00:03:05.569 --> 00:03:08.379
In the sign of three treasure is replaced
with bank gold.

00:03:08.379 --> 00:03:12.290
7 - Mary’s guardian was charles augustus
magnussen.

00:03:12.290 --> 00:03:14.799
The person who sent her the telegram addressed
CAM.

00:03:14.799 --> 00:03:19.300
That abbreviated CAM was also used by the
book villain milverton which magnussen is

00:03:19.300 --> 00:03:20.300
based on.

00:03:20.300 --> 00:03:22.829
Mind mind has been blown.

00:03:22.829 --> 00:03:28.760
8 - The telegram CAM sent said specifically,
wish you’re family could’ve seen this.

00:03:28.760 --> 00:03:33.380
Note that in the timeline of the episode the
wedding is the day after the final bank robber

00:03:33.380 --> 00:03:34.380
scene.

00:03:34.380 --> 00:03:37.010
On that day donovan was on her way to arrest
the gang.

00:03:37.010 --> 00:03:39.420
So mary’s real father could have been in
jail during the wedding.

00:03:39.420 --> 00:03:44.451
I know a lot of people believe that Mary will
die in episode 3, but if her father is one

00:03:44.451 --> 00:03:47.319
of these bank robbers, it could be him that
dies.

00:03:47.319 --> 00:03:52.200
9 - The papers fluttering when lestrade’s
backup arrives at baker street is the beginnings

00:03:52.200 --> 00:03:57.069
of sherlock’s waltz for john and mary. that
you later see him dancing to when mrs hudson

00:03:57.069 --> 00:03:58.069
brings morning tea.

00:03:58.069 --> 00:04:01.849
Later at the wedding you learn that sherlock
loves to dance and that he taught watson how

00:04:01.849 --> 00:04:02.849
to dance.

00:04:02.849 --> 00:04:08.069
10 - Mrs hudson’s private life.

00:04:08.069 --> 00:04:12.281
We learn that mrs hudson’s husband was executed
for committing double homicide and that he

00:04:12.281 --> 00:04:14.269
was a drug dealer in florida.

00:04:14.269 --> 00:04:17.400
Everytime I look at her now I think of skylar
white.

00:04:17.400 --> 00:04:20.100
11 - Sherlock Holmes Wedding Planner.

00:04:20.100 --> 00:04:24.480
Sherlock’s nature misleads you into thinking
he’d be a terrible best man, but because

00:04:24.480 --> 00:04:29.490
he’s trying so hard to integrate into john
and mary’s new life he goes extremely overboard

00:04:29.490 --> 00:04:33.910
in managing almost every detail of their wedding,
from vetting the guest list, to helping plan

00:04:33.910 --> 00:04:37.240
the seating chart to folding napkins into
orgami swans.

00:04:37.240 --> 00:04:39.810
He really wants to be a part of their new
family.

00:04:39.810 --> 00:04:42.090
12 - Sherlock is amazing with children.

00:04:42.090 --> 00:04:43.090
Sherlock and archie’s scenes are a reference
to holmes from the books.

00:04:43.090 --> 00:04:46.090
In the original stories, holmes employed and
took care of neighborhood children.

00:04:46.090 --> 00:04:47.900
They were called the baker street irregulars.

00:04:47.900 --> 00:04:52.040
On the show they’re represented by sherlock’s
homeless network.

00:04:52.040 --> 00:04:56.700
Imagine sherlock helping raise john and mary’s
baby.

00:04:56.700 --> 00:05:00.430
13 - Also during his scenes with archie, sherlock
mentions that he’ll ask a grownup.

00:05:00.430 --> 00:05:03.440
Meaning that he thinks of himself as not being
a grown up.

00:05:03.440 --> 00:05:07.210
Another reference to the origins of the character
being something of a peter pan figure.

00:05:07.210 --> 00:05:08.900
always going on adventure.

00:05:08.900 --> 00:05:13.340
Remember that most of the original holmes
story titles were the adventure of something

00:05:13.340 --> 00:05:14.340
something.

00:05:14.340 --> 00:05:16.300
14 - Major character development.

00:05:16.300 --> 00:05:19.580
Sherlock seeking attachment is a big deal
in this episode.

00:05:19.580 --> 00:05:23.130
Notice him asking mary about john’s relationship
with major sholto.

00:05:23.130 --> 00:05:26.790
Later he argues with Mycroft about caring
being an advantage and mycroft advising him

00:05:26.790 --> 00:05:29.550
against getting involved.

00:05:29.550 --> 00:05:33.750
15 - Redbeard.

00:05:33.750 --> 00:05:37.500
So many people had questions about this, but
the best theory i’ve seen supports the idea

00:05:37.500 --> 00:05:41.510
that when mycroft mentions redbeard he’s
actually referencing mary.

00:05:41.510 --> 00:05:44.820
He says redbeard twice during their phonecall.

00:05:44.820 --> 00:05:49.360
Redbeard was a pirate with his brother who
continued being a pirate after his brother

00:05:49.360 --> 00:05:50.360
died.

00:05:50.360 --> 00:05:53.550
So on one level it’s a reference that sherlock
will have to continue solving crimes alone

00:05:53.550 --> 00:05:55.040
once watson leaves him.

00:05:55.040 --> 00:05:56.780
But here’s where it gets interesting.

00:05:56.780 --> 00:06:00.040
Redbeard had an adopted son named Eric Lerouge.

00:06:00.040 --> 00:06:02.020
Eric was a wealthy aristocrat who’s parent’s
were killed.

00:06:02.020 --> 00:06:03.020
Redbeard found him and took him in.

00:06:03.020 --> 00:06:06.100
Later Eric started living an honest life under
a different name, but Redbeard the pirate

00:06:06.100 --> 00:06:10.170
kept coming back into his life asking him
for help with new schemes.

00:06:10.170 --> 00:06:12.441
If magnussen is the master blackmailer that
his book version milverton was, what if magnussen

00:06:12.441 --> 00:06:17.530
is the redbeard that mycroft is talking about
and he keeps blackmailing mary morstan.

00:06:17.530 --> 00:06:19.790
who in this case would be the eric character.

00:06:19.790 --> 00:06:23.680
That theory doesn’t invoke the bank robber
plot I mentioned earlier, but mark gatiss

00:06:23.680 --> 00:06:27.640
teased episode 3 by posting this tweet, which
only said “redbeard”.

00:06:27.640 --> 00:06:30.660
meaning that idea is central to the plot of
his last vow.

00:06:30.660 --> 00:06:31.730
Everything is connected.

00:06:31.730 --> 00:06:33.670
there are no coincidences.

00:06:33.670 --> 00:06:36.160
16 - Mycroft working out.

00:06:36.160 --> 00:06:40.260
This was hilarious but in addition to teasing
mycroft’s ring, redbeard and sherlock’s

00:06:40.260 --> 00:06:44.630
childhood it’s also a reference to the original
mycroft being described as very fat.

00:06:44.630 --> 00:06:48.240
I already discussed mycroft’s ring in my
q and a video, so If you want to learn more

00:06:48.240 --> 00:06:51.900
about that I’ll add a link at the end of
the video.

00:06:51.900 --> 00:06:55.270
17 - Sherlock asks mycroft to come to the
wedding again.

00:06:55.270 --> 00:06:59.250
This ties into the idea that mycroft knows
more about mary than he’s letting on and

00:06:59.250 --> 00:07:03.880
is advising sherlock not to get involved so
he won’t be there when she comes between

00:07:03.880 --> 00:07:06.280
mycroft the government and charles augustus
magnussen.

00:07:06.280 --> 00:07:07.850
If sherlock gets too involved with mary and
mycroft tries to take her down for being involved

00:07:07.850 --> 00:07:08.850
with the villain, then mycroft would have
to take sherlock down too.

00:07:08.850 --> 00:07:11.940
Does sherlock’s last vow include protecting
mary from mycroft?

00:07:11.940 --> 00:07:15.800
Notice how when the camera cuts back and forth
between them they each turn to face away from

00:07:15.800 --> 00:07:16.800
each other.

00:07:16.800 --> 00:07:18.750
18 - Sherlock’s Toast.

00:07:18.750 --> 00:07:21.540
The toast itself is the backbone of the whole
episode.

00:07:21.540 --> 00:07:24.820
all the other flashbacks and stories branch
off and come back to it.

00:07:24.820 --> 00:07:27.350
But there are several cannon references during
it.

00:07:27.350 --> 00:07:31.310
namely sherlock borrowing the “I can’t
congratulate you” line from watson’s character

00:07:31.310 --> 00:07:32.410
in the book scandal in bohemia.

00:07:32.410 --> 00:07:35.720
Then there’s the funny stories, there were
book references, mostly to things from sign

00:07:35.720 --> 00:07:41.110
of four including the poison giant, then there
was the hollow client, the inexplicable matchbox,

00:07:41.110 --> 00:07:44.550
the blanched soldier, the case of identity
and the vanishing elephant.

00:07:44.550 --> 00:07:46.440
He also references mary’s bridesmaid with
the great beauty line.

00:07:46.440 --> 00:07:48.860
It’s a book reference to the character maud
bellamy.

00:07:48.860 --> 00:07:51.390
19 - Molly is Sherlock’s Dana Sculley.

00:07:51.390 --> 00:07:55.330
Molly’s montage was hilarious, but her and
sherlock’s interactions really invoked a

00:07:55.330 --> 00:07:59.960
classic x files mulder and sculley vibe.

00:07:59.960 --> 00:08:01.610
Drunk science for the win.

00:08:01.610 --> 00:08:04.910
20 - The first telegram was from Mike stamford.

00:08:04.910 --> 00:08:08.650
The person who introduced watson to sherlock
during study in pink.

00:08:08.650 --> 00:08:12.170
21 - Notice Mary’s face when sherlock says
the name CAM.

00:08:12.170 --> 00:08:15.080
reinforcing the idea that mary is afraid of
him.

00:08:15.080 --> 00:08:19.650
Also rewind to my numbers 5 through 7 for
more evidence that she’s being blackmailed.

00:08:19.650 --> 00:08:22.540
22 - Watson asks sherlock to be his best man.

00:08:22.540 --> 00:08:24.940
This was the scene that they showed at comic
con.

00:08:24.940 --> 00:08:28.250
Notice that watson does not stop sherlock
from drinking the eyeball tea.

00:08:28.250 --> 00:08:32.690
23 - When sherlock says sorry for that last
one, that’s his subtle way of apologizing

00:08:32.690 --> 00:08:34.080
for faking his death.

00:08:34.080 --> 00:08:36.959
Q24 - They’re planning the wedding at baker
street.

00:08:36.959 --> 00:08:42.529
Normally they’d plan it at mary’s, but
they want sherlock to be a part of their family

00:08:42.529 --> 00:08:44.470
they bring the wedding to him.

00:08:44.470 --> 00:08:46.470
25 - Sherlock is youtubing.

00:08:46.470 --> 00:08:49.889
This was funny, but it also lets us know that
mary can deduce emotions the same way sherlock

00:08:49.889 --> 00:08:50.970
deduces clues.

00:08:50.970 --> 00:08:53.970
She always knows when someone is lying.

00:08:53.970 --> 00:08:57.329
26 - The bloody guardsmen is dean thomas from
harry potter

00:08:57.329 --> 00:09:01.710
27 - Watson’s interaction with the military
commander reminds us about watson’s life

00:09:01.710 --> 00:09:03.500
beyond Sherlock Holmes.

00:09:03.500 --> 00:09:06.040
In the holmes books, most of sherlock’s
past is still a mystery.

00:09:06.040 --> 00:09:08.750
But we actually know a lot about watson.

00:09:08.750 --> 00:09:13.129
28 - Sherlock explains that he only solves
crimes, but watson saves lives.

00:09:13.129 --> 00:09:15.220
Talking about how he saved the guardsman.

00:09:15.220 --> 00:09:18.250
It also lets you know how he thinks of watson.

00:09:18.250 --> 00:09:22.680
29 - The barfight is a possible reference
to sign of four, where he starts a bar fight

00:09:22.680 --> 00:09:24.350
just to get information.

00:09:24.350 --> 00:09:29.980
30 - At the point of the stairs, mrs hudson
reveals that they had only been out drinking

00:09:29.980 --> 00:09:30.980
for two hours.

00:09:30.980 --> 00:09:35.310
31 - Am I the current king of england is a
joke referencing the original character.

00:09:35.310 --> 00:09:38.660
In that character’s study there was a picture
of queen victoria on the wall, when there

00:09:38.660 --> 00:09:39.660
was no king.

00:09:39.660 --> 00:09:40.660
Just like in present day england.

00:09:40.660 --> 00:09:44.139
Benedict Cumberbatch’s version even shot
her initials into the wall when he got bored.

00:09:44.139 --> 00:09:48.110
32 - The game is something, one of the best
jokes in the episode.

00:09:48.110 --> 00:09:51.160
33 - The chat room mind palace.

00:09:51.160 --> 00:09:54.870
Sherlock deduces the mayfly man by clueing
for looks from the chat room women.

00:09:54.870 --> 00:09:58.560
The scene is beautifully shot and incorporates
some freudian imagery.

00:09:58.560 --> 00:10:02.629
Sherlock is a very cerebral show, and freud
talked about the id, the ego and the super

00:10:02.629 --> 00:10:03.629
ego.

00:10:03.629 --> 00:10:04.629
Inside the mind palace sherlock talks with
both watson and mycroft like he talks to ghost

00:10:04.629 --> 00:10:05.629
watson in empty hearse.

00:10:05.629 --> 00:10:09.960
Inside the mind palace mycroft represents
the id, the super rational portion of sherlock’s

00:10:09.960 --> 00:10:11.980
brain.

00:10:11.980 --> 00:10:16.089
Watson represents the super ego, the part
of his brain that deals with emotions.

00:10:16.089 --> 00:10:20.730
Sherlock himself represents the ego, the part
that helps the id and the superego communicate.

00:10:20.730 --> 00:10:23.449
That’s why mycroft is yelling at him.

00:10:23.449 --> 00:10:31.589
In case you didn’t catch it, all of the
women worked near colonel sholto.

00:10:31.589 --> 00:10:35.470
34 - The cigarrettes he’s hiding in his
slipper is a reference to the book holmes

00:10:35.470 --> 00:10:38.129
hiding tobacco in his persian slippers.

00:10:38.129 --> 00:10:40.529
35 - Sherlock is broken.

00:10:40.529 --> 00:10:46.629
He exhibits signs of PTSD as his mind palace
hasn’t been functioning at 100 percent this

00:10:46.629 --> 00:10:47.629
series.

00:10:47.629 --> 00:10:49.600
He also has to physically abuse himself to
focus.

00:10:49.600 --> 00:10:53.720
It’s possible that something dark happened
to him during the two years he was alone that

00:10:53.720 --> 00:10:55.069
he hasn’t dealt with yet.

00:10:55.069 --> 00:10:57.410
36 - Sherlock’s last vow.

00:10:57.410 --> 00:11:01.360
He vows to protect watson’s new family,
but it sounds like that will eventually put

00:11:01.360 --> 00:11:03.370
him in opposition to mycroft.

00:11:03.370 --> 00:11:05.959
And in the books, watson did not have any
children.

00:11:05.959 --> 00:11:07.740
Which is a poor omen for episode 3.

00:11:07.740 --> 00:11:11.190
and 37 a doctor who reference.

00:11:11.190 --> 00:11:14.839
Notice that sherlock leaving the wedding early
looks very similar to the doctor trying to

00:11:14.839 --> 00:11:17.220
leave amy and rory’s wedding during the
big bang.

00:11:17.220 --> 00:11:22.509
It’s another case of a very strange man
or timelord trying to leave when he feels

00:11:22.509 --> 00:11:24.019
he’s the odd one out.

00:11:24.019 --> 00:11:28.180
Amy and rory chased after the doctor, and
even though john and mary didn’t chase sherlock.

00:11:28.180 --> 00:11:31.569
they’ve spent the entire episode trying
to make him feel like he is part of their

00:11:31.569 --> 00:11:32.850
new family.

00:11:32.850 --> 00:11:37.589
So lots of theories came out of a few big
clues namely mary’s real identity, her connection

00:11:37.589 --> 00:11:40.870
to the villain and the bank robbers.

00:11:40.870 --> 00:11:46.470
Let me know if there were any other big clues
you saw or cool references to book canon.

00:11:46.470 --> 00:11:52.630
One really big thing I’ll end on is that
episode 3 ties together so many plots that

00:11:52.630 --> 00:11:53.750
everyone who has seen it is going crazy.

00:11:53.750 --> 00:11:55.860
Stephen moffat said the cliffhanger is even
worse than series 2.

00:11:55.860 --> 00:11:59.800
Series 3 essentially becomes the story of
everything that happened from series 1 up

00:11:59.800 --> 00:12:00.800
to now.

00:12:00.800 --> 00:12:04.420
Meaning that Moriarty, The Bank Robbers, The
Tube Bombing, Mary Morstan and Charles Augustus

00:12:04.420 --> 00:12:06.910
Milverton are all connected.

00:12:06.910 --> 00:12:09.040
Be sure to subscribe to get more of my sherlock
videos.

00:12:09.040 --> 00:12:13.300
my next one will be a review of episode 3
this sunday.

00:12:13.300 --> 00:12:16.649
